  "result": "Fixed. Subcommands now read their defaults from their own entry in `default_map`.\n\n**Cause:** In `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py`, around line 392), a subcommand's context inherited the parent's entire `default_map`. So for `{\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}`, the `runserver` command looked up `port` at the top level and never found it. The fix takes the sub-dictionary keyed by the subcommand's name:\n\n```python\ndefault_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n- The reported case now gives `5000` instead of the parameter default `8000`. A CLI value still wins (`--port 7` gives `7`).\n- I added `test_default_map_nested_for_subcommand` to `tests/test_defaults.py`. It fails without the fix and passes with it.\n- Full suite: 1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n\nI did not add a `CHANGES.md` entry. If you want one, I can add it under the unreleased section.",
